DevLog 3 05/08/2026
In this devlog, I want to show you three updates:

I’ve made the supports more modular and easily detachable from the main panel, so if one breaks, I can easily replace it. I’ve also started designing them with a pull system similar to the real A320 FCU.
I’ve created the rear panel, which will also be very modular. It will be mounted using a slot with two rails behind it and will be held in place by the upper panel.
I corrected the positions of three knobs because I realized that their measurements were incorrect. I adjusted their positions to make the layout more accurate and closer to the real A320 FCU.
WHAT TO EXPECT IN DEVLOG 5:
-Upper panel, as similar as possible to the real thing

-Start or finish the knob pull system, which will be spring-loaded

-Continue improving the modular design
